python-opentelemetry-api (1.41.1-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix debian/py3dist-overrides: map importlib_metadata to
    python3-importlib-metadata instead of bare python3. The previous
    mapping assumed Python 3.12+ stdlib importlib.metadata satisfies
    `import importlib_metadata`, but that's a distinct top-level backport
    package (python3-importlib-metadata, a real installable package in
    trixie), not a stdlib submodule. This silently dropped the real
    Depends, causing ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
    'importlib_metadata' at runtime (mcp-server-webdriver issue #3)

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0200
